-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  dir_outputpath.pcpp - Directive compliance: @outputpath

  @outputpath "<path>"; sets the folder the build writes to (the generated
  C++, zig's folders, the program), in the main module only (BNF.md sec 2).
  It resolves once, as every path directive ($P: = the folder pcpp.exe is
  in), so the CLI and the editor build in the same place. pcpp -o wins over
  it; without either the folder is output. dll_build.pcpp depends on it:
  it links its dll from the folder the dll's @outputpath names.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\dir_outputpath.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\dir_outputpath.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    built where the source says
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 0
  The [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.
  CHECK: output\dir_outputpath_out\zig-out\bin holds the program (output\dir_outputpath_out_linux
  for the Linux build).

  Break it: run each file below the same way, without -r; each reports
  exactly what the // comment on its marked line says, and nothing else:
    dir_outputpath_err_twice.pcpp   @outputpath given twice
    dir_outputpath_err_shape.pcpp   its value is a string
*******************************************************************************/

module exe dir_outputpath;
@ifdef TARGET_X86_64_LINUX_GNU
@outputpath "$P:output/dir_outputpath_out_linux";
@else
@outputpath "$P:output/dir_outputpath_out";
@endif

begin
  println("built where the source says");
end.
